<deck title="the align attribute" />

# The global `align` attribute

`align="left | center | right"` works on **every** component — images, code,
diagrams, animations, and live shells.

Centered is the default (prose and code default to the flush-left text column).

---

## Three images, three alignments

<img src="sample.png" width="20" align="left" />

<img src="sample.png" width="20" align="center" />

<img src="sample.png" width="20" align="right" />

---

## Code, pushed right

A `<code>` block normally sits in the flush-left text column; `align="right"` floats it to the right edge instead.

<code lang="rust" align="right">
fn main() {
    println!("hi");
}
</code>

---

## A diagram, pulled left

A `<mermaid>` diagram is centered by default; `align="left"` moves it over.

<mermaid align="left">
flowchart LR
  A --> B --> C
</mermaid>

---

## A live shell, right

<tty align="right" title="clock" rows="4" cols="22">
while :; do date "+%H:%M:%S"; sleep 1; done
</tty>
